From 21a89192e8dbe4bfc2c61bad3ae7868683b0db2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:19:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dos: pick the largest same-aspect VESA mode ourselves,
 not SDL's smallest-first tie-break

Root-caused during the 2026-09 benchmark campaign (docs/BENCHMARK-PLAN.md,
mach64-215ct-2026-09-03.md): a real-hardware ATI Mach64 launch landed on
512x384 instead of the requested 320x240, because that card has no
native 320x240 mode and SDL3's own SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode
tie-breaks same-aspect-ratio candidates (320x240/512x384/640x480 are
all exactly 4:3) by always keeping the smallest. Visible on camera as
green dashed banding above the title logo -- leftover VRAM/text-mode
content in a mode this port had never actually validated before.

The only standing mitigation was an ad hoc "SET SDL_HINT_DOS_FORCE_MODE_ID=
0x0111" before each manual benchmark launch, never baked into the
shipped binary -- fine for a controlled benchmark session, not for a
normal player just running DOSSAGE.EXE. A hardcoded FORCE_MODE_ID can't
be baked in unconditionally either: Cirrus and ViRGE both have an exact
320x240 match already and would be actively broken by forcing them onto
640x480 too.

Fix instead by enumerating available modes ourselves before creating
the window: if the exact request isn't there, pick the largest
same-aspect candidate rather than trusting the closest-match tie-break,
and request its exact dimensions (no tie left to break). Cards with an
exact match are untouched -- this block is a no-op for them.

This is a dossage-local workaround, not a shared-layer fix -- doskutsu
hits the identical SDL3 tie-break on the identical card and carries the
same ad hoc-only mitigation (its own docs/internal/BOOT.md). The
general case (SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode's tie-break itself)
would be worth fixing once in the hub's shared SDL3-DOS layer rather
than per-port, but that is a separate, cross-port change; this patch
only unblocks dossage's own real-hardware behavior.

Not yet independently re-confirmed on real Mach64 hardware -- DOSBox-X's
own emulated VESA BIOS (S3 Trio64) has a native 320x240 mode and so
cannot reproduce this exact tie-break; DOSBox-X smoke testing here only
confirms no regression on cards that already had an exact match.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 62 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 62 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index f506c70..c65f6af 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -621,6 +621,68 @@ void createScreen() {
     flags = flags | SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN;
     displayW = screenWidth;
     displayH = screenHeight;
+
+    // DOS-PORT: work around SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode's own
+    // aspect-ratio tie-break (see SDL_HINT_DOS_FORCE_MODE_ID's doc comment
+    // in SDL_hints.h) always keeping the SMALLEST same-aspect candidate
+    // when the exact requested mode isn't enumerated. Real-hardware
+    // finding (2026-09 benchmark campaign, docs/BENCHMARK-PLAN.md): a card
+    // with no native mode matching screenWidth/screenHeight -- e.g. ATI
+    // Mach64, which has no 320x240 -- lands on a smaller same-aspect
+    // fallback (512x384) instead of the intended larger one (640x480),
+    // visible as leftover-VRAM green corruption above the title logo in
+    // that never-before-cleared mode. Cards with an exact match (Cirrus,
+    // ViRGE) hit no tie at all and are untouched by this block.
+    //
+    // Fix: enumerate the actually-available modes ourselves before
+    // creating the window. If the exact request isn't among them, pick
+    // the LARGEST same-aspect-ratio candidate instead of trusting the
+    // closest-match tie-break, and request that mode's exact dimensions
+    // -- an exact request has no tie to break.
+    {
+        int numModes = 0;
+        SDL_DisplayMode **modes = SDL_GetFullscreenDisplayModes(
+            SDL_GetPrimaryDisplay(), &numModes );
+
+        if( modes != NULL ) {
+            bool exactMatch = false;
+            for( int i=0; i<numModes && !exactMatch; i++ ) {
+                if( modes[i]->w == displayW && modes[i]->h == displayH ) {
+                    exactMatch = true;
+                    }
+                }
+
+            if( !exactMatch ) {
+                double targetAspect = (double)displayW / (double)displayH;
+                int bestW = 0;
+                int bestH = 0;
+
+                for( int i=0; i<numModes; i++ ) {
+                    int w = modes[i]->w;
+                    int h = modes[i]->h;
+                    double aspect = (double)w / (double)h;
+
+                    if( fabs( aspect - targetAspect ) < 0.001 &&
+                        w * h > bestW * bestH ) {
+                        bestW = w;
+                        bestH = h;
+                        }
+                    }
+
+                if( bestW > 0 &&
+                    ( bestW > displayW || bestH > displayH ) ) {
+                    printf( "DOS-PORT: no exact %dx%d mode -- using "
+                            "largest same-aspect alternative %dx%d "
+                            "instead of the smallest-first tie-break\n",
+                            displayW, displayH, bestW, bestH );
+                    displayW = bestW;
+                    displayH = bestH;
+                    }
+                }
+
+            SDL_free( modes );
+            }
+    }
 #endif
 
     window = SDL_CreateWindow( "Passage", displayW, displayH, flags );
-- 
